{"id": "EUVD-2026-38816", "enisaUuid": "ef03d009-c5ff-381e-810b-8dd764d9910d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: dev: prevent integer overflow in I2C_TIMEOUT ioctl\n\nWhile fuzzing with Syzkaller, a persistent `schedule_timeout: wrong\ntimeout value` warning was observed, accompanied by SMBus controller\nstate machine corruption.\n\nThe I2C_TIMEOUT ioctl accepts a user-provided timeout in multiples of\n10 ms. The user argument is checked against INT_MAX, but it is\nsubsequently multiplied by 10 before being passed to msecs_to_jiffies().\n\nA malicious user can pass a large value (e.g., 429496729) that passes\nthe `arg > INT_MAX` check but overflows when multiplied by 10. This\nresults in a truncated 32-bit unsigned value that bypasses the\ninternal `(int)m < 0` check in `msecs_to_jiffies()`.\n\nThe truncated value is then assigned to `client->adapter->timeout`\n(a signed 32-bit int), which is reinterpreted as a negative number.\nWhen passed to wait_for_completion_timeout(), this negative value\nundergoes sign extension to a 64-bit unsigned long, triggering the\n`schedule_timeout` warning and causing premature returns. This leaves\nthe SMBus state machine in an unrecoverable state, constituting a\nlocal Denial of Service (DoS).\n\nFix this by bounding the user argument to `INT_MAX / 10`.\n\n[wsa: move the comment as well]", "datePublished": "2026-06-24T16:26:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:22:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9ffd5f5050fbb199d270a85614cd27ebed6fbac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b88ecfbc9dc33b4db8836c37b50cf174e6c0691", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/943e318eedbeaeea08ece3f5dd44c982f4ed2ef5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa6ef734016912653a909477fb30aeb66c98b3a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff02add34ffd03449b8115904ebe2ec4fed022d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffbcf31f032eb454ebfd29309f51366fe57f4ac4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4576621dc6577f21a032acfd16c3ad61907a5ea7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/617eb7c0961a8dfcfc811844a6396e406b2923ea"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rj5f-9xf7-69h7", "CVE-2026-52948"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09ba1971-1785-38c4-b916-b8b4f2e9cd09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd97f39b7cdf1c8a9c9f52865eec795b7f0c811d <aa6ef734016912653a909477fb30aeb66c98b3a2"}, {"id": "0f942e4f-d934-36f8-9e25-6c810c12d4c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.176"}, {"id": "15af4b0f-c1b3-3c5e-8e8a-a74c63639c6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5a0e54d1-ba7a-3ded-98a0-265a11c01e13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "901e0a5f-5ac9-3f01-aacc-f014e083d9ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd97f39b7cdf1c8a9c9f52865eec795b7f0c811d <ffbcf31f032eb454ebfd29309f51366fe57f4ac4"}, {"id": "91f6358a-9427-3765-9b41-b9309cb96550", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd97f39b7cdf1c8a9c9f52865eec795b7f0c811d <ff02add34ffd03449b8115904ebe2ec4fed022d4"}, {"id": "9b5ed0de-8981-3118-8f2c-4c01b6952137", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.143"}, {"id": "9d5e2b8a-e790-3958-b899-138e87ae668e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd97f39b7cdf1c8a9c9f52865eec795b7f0c811d <0b88ecfbc9dc33b4db8836c37b50cf174e6c0691"}, {"id": "9e26c620-909a-3d25-9959-fd1a3e51fdd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd97f39b7cdf1c8a9c9f52865eec795b7f0c811d <4576621dc6577f21a032acfd16c3ad61907a5ea7"}, {"id": "b15312ad-0777-3b97-a3bd-74c71a795cd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd97f39b7cdf1c8a9